    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #320\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-228-agent-runtime-01-08-persist-agent-life-thr_7g8jw5h4py`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #228 ([agent-runtime 01/08] Persist agent lifecycle events):\n\n- **Migration** `0013_agent_run_events.sql`: adds the `agent_run_events` turn-level log table (bigserial cursor, FK to `agent_runs`, `kind` CHECK-constrained to `turn_start`/`message`/`tool_use`/`tool_result`/`turn_end`/`run_status`, `payload jsonb`) plus its `(agent_run_id, id)` index.\n- **`agentRunEventsStore.ts`** in `@semprec/data`: `insertAgentRunEvent` / `listAgentRunEvents` (ordered by `id ASC` for monotonic reconstruction), exported from the package's public entry point.\n- **New `packages/agent-runtime` package**: a `runAgentSession()` adapter that creates the `agent_runs` row on start, consumes an ordered sequence of `AgentMessage`s, persists one `agent_run_events` row per lifecycle event, drops `message_update` streaming deltas entirely, and finalizes `agent_runs` (status/result snapshot/`finished_at`) on completion or error. `unit` defaults to `'invocation'` with `'session'` selectable by the caller.\n\nSince the external `pi-agent-core` package has no published API yet (it's an empty npm placeholder), the adapter models its expected shape as a local TypeScript contract and takes `createAgentSession` as an injected dependency — this keeps the wrapper fully buildable and testable now, with a one-line wiring change needed once the real package ships matching types.\n\n**Verification:** build clean across all workspace packages, dependency-boundary check clean, migration-numbering check clean, unit tests 83/83, integration tests 407/407 (confirmed one transient failure during a mid-session run was pre-existing, unrelated flakiness in an untouched concurrency test — reproduced passing on immediate re-run), e2e tests 5/5.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
